## Understanding the Code

The CUDA kernel `row_scan_kernel` performs a cumulative sum (prefix sum) along rows. Let me trace through the code:

1. Each block processes one row (block index = row)
2. Each thread loads multiple elements (stride by blockDim.x)
3. Thread 0 performs the sequential scan
4. All threads store results back

### Original Code Flow:
```cuda
// Load row into shared memory
for (int i = tid; i < cols; i += blockDim.x) {
    shared[i] = input[row * cols + i];
}
__syncthreads();  // <-- ORIGINAL: barrier after loading

// Perform sequential scan in shared memory
if (tid == 0) {
    for (int i = 1; i < cols; i++) {
        shared[i] += shared[i - 1];
    }
}
__syncthreads();

// Store results
for (int i = tid; i < cols; i += blockDim.x) {
    output[row * cols + i] = shared[i];
}
```

